MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
Layout keywords name characters that a delimiter structure could not
otherwise spell. SPACE stands for one space and NL for a newline.
MCDEF PAIR, SPACE ; AS <[%A1.|%A2.|%A3.]>
PAIR x,y z;
A delimiter is consumed, so text after the last one follows straight on.
MCDEF TAIL, SPACE AS <[%A1.|%A2.]>
TAIL p,q rest of the line
MCDEF LINE NL AS <[%A1.]>
LINE runs to the end of its line
Done.
